2. dashboard/__tests__/chibi-quest-hero-row-type.test.ts (new, F26/F27):
   - `gives paragraph 1 the same print type as paragraph 2 (12 pt,
     line-height 2)`: renders origins-3.2 p05 with look chibi-quest,
     asserts the row markup exists and holds paragraph 1, asserts the
     template print values (`.article-text` 12pt/2), then asserts
     paragraph 1 resolves to 12pt and line-height 2 and equals paragraph 2.
     Print-media emulation uses a CSSOM style element that descends into
     `@media print`, like the existing winningProperty helper, plus DOM
     ancestry (closest `.article-text`) and any chibi-quest paragraph
     override (so either Green fix shape passes).
   - `prints the marking key before paragraph 1, as in the classic look`:
     renders the same fixture with both looks, asserts the classic legend
     precedes classic paragraph 1, then asserts the chibi legend precedes
     chibi paragraph 1. Indices use `class="marking-legend"` and
     `para-number">N` markup hooks, never stylesheet text. Positive guards
     (legend found, paragraph 1 found, classic order holds) precede the
     chibi order assertion, so the check cannot pass vacuously.
   - `finds the row markup without matching the stylesheet text` (F28
     guard, passes at HEAD): a synthetic document whose `<style>` block
     holds an unescaped `.chibi-hero-row` selector still resolves to the
     `<div class="chibi-hero-row">` markup, which holds the hero and no
     `<style>` text.
